Evidence: demos had 2x2 same-color marker-corner rectangles mapping to a single output cell (demo 3: 0, 6, 9, 4; demo 2: 0/3), while unmarked or mixed-corner cells used the large-grid interior fill. Test output was a 3x6 grid, correctly derived by this rule. Treat this as a pattern clue, not a universal rule absent matching lattice evidence."
